/-!
# Lazard's theorem

Let `R` be a commutative ring and `M` an `R`-module. Then `M` is flat if and only if `M` is
the colimit of a directed system of free finite `R`-modules.

## Notation

An `R`-module `M` is flat when `- ⊗_R M` is exact, equivalently when `f ⊗ id_M` is
injective for every injective `R`-linear `f : N → N'`; this is `Module.Flat`. A module is
free and finite when it is isomorphic to `Rⁿ` for some `n`, i.e. satisfies both
`Module.Free R P` and `Module.Finite R P`.

A directed system of `R`-modules consists of a directed, nonempty, filtered index preorder
`(ι, ≤)`, a family of `R`-modules `F i`, and transition maps `φ_{ij} : F i → F j` for
`i ≤ j` with `φ_{ii} = id` and `φ_{jk} ∘ φ_{ij} = φ_{ik}` — the conditions bundled as
`DirectedSystem`. Its colimit is `(⨁_i F i) / S`, with `S` generated by the elements
`ι_i(x) − ι_j(φ_{ij}(x))` for `i ≤ j` and `x ∈ F i`; in Mathlib this is
`Module.DirectLimit`. Saying `M` is the colimit of a directed system of free finite
`R`-modules means there is such a system with every `F i` free and finite together with an
`R`-linear isomorphism `colim_{i ∈ ι} F i ≅ M`.

## Proof outline

The direction (⇐) holds because a directed colimit of flat modules is flat: directed
colimits are exact and commute with tensor products, and free finite modules are flat.

The direction (⇒) is the substantive content. An arbitrary module is written as the
directed colimit of the finitely presented quotients `R^J / N` indexed by pairs `(J, N)`,
and when `M` is flat the indices for which `R^J / N` is free form a cofinal subset; the
input for that step is the factorization lemma
`Module.Flat.iff_forall_exists_factorization`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open Module in
/-- Lifting a finite family of elements of a directed colimit to a common index. -/
theorem Module.DirectLimit.exists_of_fin {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {ι : Type*} [Preorder ι]
    [IsDirected ι (· ≤ ·)] [Nonempty ι] [DecidableEq ι] {G : ι → Type*}
    [(i : ι) → AddCommGroup (G i)] [(i : ι) → Module R (G i)]
    {f : (i j : ι) → i ≤ j → G i →ₗ[R] G j} (l : ℕ) (x : Fin l → Module.DirectLimit G f) :
    ∃ (j : ι) (y : Fin l → G j), ∀ i, Module.DirectLimit.of R ι G f j (y i) = x i := by
  choose js ys hys using fun i => Module.DirectLimit.exists_of (x i)
  obtain ⟨J, hJ⟩ := Finset.exists_le (Finset.image js Finset.univ)
  refine ⟨J, fun i => f (js i) J (hJ _ (by simp)) (ys i), fun i => ?_⟩
  rw [Module.DirectLimit.of_f]
  exact hys i

open Module in
/-- A directed colimit of flat modules is flat. -/
theorem Module.Flat.directLimit {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {ι : Type*} [Preorder ι]
    [IsDirected ι (· ≤ ·)] [Nonempty ι] [DecidableEq ι] {G : ι → Type*}
    [(i : ι) → AddCommGroup (G i)] [(i : ι) → Module R (G i)]
    {f : (i j : ι) → i ≤ j → G i →ₗ[R] G j} [DirectedSystem G (fun i j h => f i j h)]
    [∀ i, Module.Flat R (G i)] :
    Module.Flat R (Module.DirectLimit G f) := by
  rw [Module.Flat.iff_forall_isTrivialRelation]
  intro l c x hx
  obtain ⟨j, y, hy⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.exists_of_fin l x
  have hsum : Module.DirectLimit.of R ι G f j (∑ i, c i • y i) = 0 := by
    rw [map_sum]; simp only [map_smul, hy]; exact hx
  obtain ⟨j', hjj', hj'⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.of.zero_exact hsum
  set z : Fin l → G j' := fun i => f j j' hjj' (y i) with hz
  have hzrel : ∑ i, c i • z i = 0 := by
    rw [hz]; simp only [← map_smul, ← map_sum]; simpa using hj'
  obtain ⟨k, a, w, hw1, hw2⟩ :=
    (Module.Flat.iff_forall_isTrivialRelation.mp inferInstance) hzrel
  refine ⟨k, a, fun jj => Module.DirectLimit.of R ι G f j' (w jj), fun i => ?_, hw2⟩
  have hxi : x i = Module.DirectLimit.of R ι G f j' (z i) := by
    rw [hz, Module.DirectLimit.of_f, hy]
  rw [hxi, hw1 i, map_sum]; simp only [map_smul]

/-!
## Forward direction (⇒): structure of the proof

This is the substantive content of Lazard's theorem: given that `M` is flat, exhibit a
directed system of free finite modules whose colimit is `M`.

### The directed system

Fix the canonical surjection from the free module on the underlying set of `M`:
`π : (M →₀ R) →ₗ[R] M`, `π = Finsupp.linearCombination R id`, with `K := ker π`.
Then `M ≃ₗ (M →₀ R) / K`.

Index the system by pairs `(J, N)` where:
  * `J ⊆ M` is a finite subset (so `R^J := J →₀ R`, equivalently the submodule of
    `M →₀ R` of functions supported in `J`, a free finite module), and
  * `N` is a finitely generated submodule of `R^J` with `N ⊆ K ∩ R^J`.
Order: `(J, N) ≤ (J', N')` iff `J ⊆ J'` and `N` maps into `N'` under the
inclusion `R^J ↪ R^J'`. The component module is the finitely presented quotient
`F (J,N) := R^J / N`, with transition maps the induced quotient maps, and a
compatible map `R^J / N → M` (well defined because `N ⊆ K`).

This index set is nonempty, witnessed by `(∅, 0)`, and directed: given `(J₁,N₁)` and
`(J₂,N₂)`, take `J := J₁ ∪ J₂` and `N := N₁ + N₂` (images in `R^J`), still finitely
generated and inside `K`.

### `M` is the colimit of this system (independent of flatness)

The induced map `colim_{(J,N)} R^J/N → M` is an isomorphism for any module `M`:
  * surjective: every `m ∈ M` is `π(δ_m)`, the image of `δ_m ∈ R^{{m}} / 0`;
  * injective: if a class at `(J,N)` maps to `0` in `M`, its lift `v ∈ R^J` lies
    in `K`; since `K ∩ R^J` is the increasing union of its f.g. submodules, the
    f.g. submodule `N' := N + R·v ⊆ K ∩ R^J` gives `(J,N) ≤ (J,N')` killing the
    class, so it is already `0` in the colimit (use
    `Module.DirectLimit.exists_eq_of_of_eq` / `of.zero_exact`).
This realizes `M` as a directed colimit of finitely presented modules.

### Flatness ⇒ free indices are cofinal

This is where flatness enters, through the factorization lemma
`Module.Flat.exists_factorization_of_apply_eq_zero_of_free`. A finitely presented
`R^J / N` is the cokernel data of a map `g : R^m →ₗ R^J` given by generators of `N`, with
`π ∘ (R^J ↠ M)` killing `N`. Applying the factorization lemma to the composite
`R^m → R^J → M`, which is zero, produces a factorization through a finite free module
`R^k`, i.e. an enlargement `(J,N) ≤ (J',N')` with `R^{J'}/N'` free finite. So the
sub-index set of pairs with free quotient is cofinal, and since a cofinal subsystem has
the same colimit, `M` is the directed colimit of free finite modules.

The forward direction is packaged as `flat_exists_directLimit_free_finite` below.
-/

open Module in
/-- The colimit of a directed system over a cofinal sub-preorder `{i // P i}` is `R`-linearly
isomorphic to the colimit over the whole index. -/
theorem Module.DirectLimit.nonempty_linearEquiv_of_cofinal {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {ι : Type u}
    [Preorder ι]
    [IsDirected ι (· ≤ ·)] [Nonempty ι] [DecidableEq ι] {G : ι → Type u}
    [(i : ι) → AddCommGroup (G i)] [(i : ι) → Module R (G i)]
    {f : (i j : ι) → i ≤ j → G i →ₗ[R] G j} [DirectedSystem G (fun i j h => f i j h)]
    (P : ι → Prop) [DecidableEq {i : ι // P i}]
    [IsDirected {i : ι // P i} (· ≤ ·)] [Nonempty {i : ι // P i}]
    (hcof : ∀ i : ι, ∃ j : ι, P j ∧ i ≤ j) :
    Nonempty
      (Module.DirectLimit (ι := {i : ι // P i})
        (fun i => G i.1) (fun i j h => f i.1 j.1 h) ≃ₗ[R]
       Module.DirectLimit G f) := by
  set Gsub : {i : ι // P i} → Type u := fun i => G i.val with hGsub
  set fsub : (i j : {i : ι // P i}) → i ≤ j → Gsub i →ₗ[R] Gsub j :=
    fun i j h => f i.val j.val h with hfsub
  -- Forward map
  let Φ : Module.DirectLimit Gsub fsub →ₗ[R] Module.DirectLimit G f :=
    Module.DirectLimit.lift R {i : ι // P i} Gsub fsub
      (fun i => Module.DirectLimit.of R ι G f i.val)
      (fun i j hij x => Module.DirectLimit.of_f)
  refine ⟨LinearEquiv.ofBijective Φ ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · -- injective
    rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨c, v, rfl⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.exists_of z
    rw [Module.DirectLimit.lift_of] at hz
    obtain ⟨d, hcd, hfv⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.of.zero_exact hz
    -- hfv : f c.1 d hcd v = 0
    obtain ⟨c', hc'P, hdc'⟩ := hcof d
    have hcc' : c ≤ (⟨c', hc'P⟩ : {i : ι // P i}) := hcd.trans hdc'
    have hkey : fsub c ⟨c', hc'P⟩ hcc' v = 0 := by
      show f c.val c' hcc' v = 0
      rw [← DirectedSystem.map_map (F := G) (f := fun i j h => f i j h) hcd hdc' v, hfv,
        map_zero]
    rw [← Module.DirectLimit.of_f (hij := hcc'), hkey, map_zero]
  · -- surjective
    intro z
    obtain ⟨i, v, rfl⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.exists_of z
    obtain ⟨j, hjP, hij⟩ := hcof i
    refine ⟨Module.DirectLimit.of R {i : ι // P i} Gsub fsub ⟨j, hjP⟩ (f i j hij v), ?_⟩
    rw [Module.DirectLimit.lift_of]
    exact Module.DirectLimit.of_f

/-! ### The concrete `(J,N)` system

The index `LazIdx R M` consists of pairs `(J,N)` with `J` finite and `N ⊆ ker π ∩ R^J`
finitely generated, where `π` is the canonical projection onto `M`. The component is
`LazIdx.Comp σ = R^J / N`, and the transition maps `LazIdx.transition` are canonical coordinate
inclusions `R^J ↪ R^{J'}` composed with quotient projections. The main statements are
`LazIdx.nonempty_directLimit_linearEquiv` (the colimit is `M`) and
`LazIdx.exists_free_finite_le` (for flat `M`, free finite components are cofinal).
-/

section LazardSystem

open Module

/-- Index for the `(J,N)` system. The ambient free module is `(M × ℕ) →₀ R`, so every
`m : M` has countably many spare basis copies `(m, n)` for `n : ℕ`. The projection
`π = Finsupp.linearCombination R Prod.fst` sends `e_{(m,n)} ↦ m` for every `n`, hence is
surjective, and the spare copies supply fresh basis indices for the cofinality step
`LazIdx.exists_free_finite_le`.

Here `J ⊆ M × ℕ` is finite and `N` is a finitely generated submodule of `(M × ℕ) →₀ R`
contained in `ker π` and supported on `J`. -/
structure LazIdx (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] where
  /-- The finite set of indices `J ⊆ M × ℕ`. -/
  J : Finset (M × ℕ)
  /-- The submodule `N` of relations, a finitely generated submodule of `ker π` supported on
  `J`. -/
  N : Submodule R ((M × ℕ) →₀ R)
  hNfg : N.FG
  hNK : N ≤ LinearMap.ker (Finsupp.linearCombination R (Prod.fst : M × ℕ → M))
  hNJ : N ≤ Finsupp.supported R R (↑J : Set (M × ℕ))

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-- Order: `(J,N) ≤ (J',N')` iff `J ⊆ J'` and `N ≤ N'` (as submodules of the
fixed ambient `(M × ℕ) →₀ R`). -/
instance : Preorder (LazIdx R M) where
  le σ τ := σ.J ⊆ τ.J ∧ σ.N ≤ τ.N
  le_refl σ := ⟨subset_refl _, le_refl _⟩
  le_trans σ τ ρ h1 h2 := ⟨subset_trans h1.1 h2.1, le_trans h1.2 h2.2⟩

/-- The submodule `N` viewed inside the supported subspace `R^J`. -/
noncomputable def LazIdx.sub (σ : LazIdx R M) :
    Submodule R (Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))) :=
  σ.N.comap (Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))).subtype

/-- An element `v` of `R^J` lies in `LazIdx.sub σ` iff its image in `(M × ℕ) →₀ R` lies in `N`. -/
@[simp]
theorem LazIdx.mem_sub {σ : LazIdx R M} {v : Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))} :
    v ∈ LazIdx.sub σ ↔ (v : (M × ℕ) →₀ R) ∈ σ.N :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The component module `R^J / N`. -/
noncomputable abbrev LazIdx.Comp (σ : LazIdx R M) : Type u :=
  (Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))) ⧸ LazIdx.sub σ

/-- Canonical inclusion `R^J ↪ R^{J'}` of supported subspaces for `J ⊆ J'`. -/
noncomputable def LazIdx.inc {σ τ : LazIdx R M} (h : σ ≤ τ) :
    Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ)) →ₗ[R]
      Finsupp.supported R R (↑τ.J : Set (M × ℕ)) :=
  Submodule.inclusion (Finsupp.supported_mono (by exact_mod_cast h.1))

/-- The inclusion `LazIdx.inc h` carries `LazIdx.sub σ` into `LazIdx.sub τ`. -/
theorem LazIdx.inc_mem_sub {σ τ : LazIdx R M} (h : σ ≤ τ)
    (v : Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))) (hv : v ∈ LazIdx.sub σ) :
    LazIdx.inc h v ∈ LazIdx.sub τ :=
  h.2 hv

/-- Transition map `R^J/N → R^{J'}/N'`, the canonical inclusion followed by the
quotient projection. -/
noncomputable def LazIdx.transition {σ τ : LazIdx R M} (h : σ ≤ τ) :
    LazIdx.Comp σ →ₗ[R] LazIdx.Comp τ :=
  (LazIdx.sub σ).mapQ (LazIdx.sub τ) (LazIdx.inc h) (LazIdx.inc_mem_sub h)

/-- The transition map sends the class of `v` to the class of its inclusion `LazIdx.inc h v`. -/
@[simp]
theorem LazIdx.transition_mk {σ τ : LazIdx R M} (h : σ ≤ τ)
    (v : Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))) :
    LazIdx.transition h (Submodule.Quotient.mk v) = Submodule.Quotient.mk (LazIdx.inc h v) :=
  rfl

/-- The canonical map `R^J → M`: restrict `π = linearCombination Prod.fst` to `R^J`. -/
noncomputable def LazIdx.supportedToM (σ : LazIdx R M) :
    (Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))) →ₗ[R] M :=
  (Finsupp.linearCombination R (Prod.fst : M × ℕ → M)).comp
    (Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))).subtype

/-- `LazIdx.sub σ ≤ ker` of the restricted `π`, so `π` descends to `R^J/N → M`. -/
theorem LazIdx.sub_le_ker_supportedToM (σ : LazIdx R M) :
    LazIdx.sub σ ≤ LinearMap.ker (LazIdx.supportedToM σ) :=
  fun _ hv => σ.hNK hv

/-- The canonical map `R^J/N → M` induced by `π`. -/
noncomputable def LazIdx.toM (σ : LazIdx R M) : LazIdx.Comp σ →ₗ[R] M :=
  (LazIdx.sub σ).liftQ (LazIdx.supportedToM σ) (LazIdx.sub_le_ker_supportedToM σ)

/-- The map `LazIdx.toM σ` sends the class of `v` to `∑ v (m, n) • m`, the image of `v` under
`π = linearCombination Prod.fst`. -/
@[simp]
theorem LazIdx.toM_mk (σ : LazIdx R M) (v : Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))) :
    LazIdx.toM σ (Submodule.Quotient.mk v) =
      Finsupp.linearCombination R Prod.fst (v : (M × ℕ) →₀ R) :=
  rfl

/-- The index type is nonempty, witnessed by `(∅, ⊥)`. -/
instance : Nonempty (LazIdx R M) := ⟨⟨∅, ⊥, Submodule.fg_bot, bot_le, bot_le⟩⟩

/-- Decidable equality on `LazIdx R M`, given classically. -/
noncomputable instance lazDecEq : DecidableEq (LazIdx R M) := Classical.decEq _

/-- The transition maps `LazIdx.transition` form a directed system. -/
instance lazDirectedSystem :
    DirectedSystem (fun σ : LazIdx R M => LazIdx.Comp σ) (fun _ _ h => LazIdx.transition h) where
  map_self := by
    intro σ x
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
    rfl
  map_map := by
    intro k j i hij hjk x
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
    rfl

/-- `LazIdx R M` is directed: `(J₁ ∪ J₂, N₁ ⊔ N₂)` dominates `(J₁,N₁)` and `(J₂,N₂)`. -/
instance LazIdx.instIsDirected : IsDirected (LazIdx R M) (· ≤ ·) := by
  classical
  refine ⟨fun σ τ => ?_⟩
  refine ⟨⟨σ.J ∪ τ.J, σ.N ⊔ τ.N, σ.hNfg.sup τ.hNfg, sup_le σ.hNK τ.hNK,
      sup_le (le_trans σ.hNJ (Finsupp.supported_mono ?_))
        (le_trans τ.hNJ (Finsupp.supported_mono ?_))⟩,
    ⟨Finset.subset_union_left, le_sup_left⟩, ⟨Finset.subset_union_right, le_sup_right⟩⟩
  · rw [Finset.coe_union]; exact Set.subset_union_left
  · rw [Finset.coe_union]; exact Set.subset_union_right

/-- Each component `R^J/N` is finitely presented. -/
instance LazIdx.finitePresentation_comp (σ : LazIdx R M) :
    Module.FinitePresentation R (LazIdx.Comp σ) := by
  set sup := Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))
  have : Module.Free R sup :=
    Module.Free.of_equiv (Finsupp.supportedEquivFinsupp (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))).symm
  have : Module.Finite R sup :=
    Module.Finite.equiv (Finsupp.supportedEquivFinsupp (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))).symm
  have hfg : (LazIdx.sub σ).FG := by
    have key := Submodule.comapSubtypeEquivOfLe σ.hNJ
    have : Module.Finite R σ.N := Module.Finite.iff_fg.mpr σ.hNfg
    have : Module.Finite R (LazIdx.sub σ) := by
      rw [LazIdx.sub]; exact Module.Finite.equiv key.symm
    exact Module.Finite.iff_fg.mp inferInstance
  change Module.FinitePresentation R (sup ⧸ LazIdx.sub σ)
  refine Module.finitePresentation_of_free_of_surjective (LazIdx.sub σ).mkQ
    (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _) ?_
  rw [Submodule.ker_mkQ]
  exact hfg

/-- The colimit of the `(J,N)` system is `M`, for any module `M`. -/
theorem LazIdx.nonempty_directLimit_linearEquiv :
    Nonempty (Module.DirectLimit (fun σ : LazIdx R M => LazIdx.Comp σ)
      (fun _ _ h => LazIdx.transition h) ≃ₗ[R] M) := by
  classical
  have Hcompat : ∀ (σ τ : LazIdx R M) (h : σ ≤ τ) (x : LazIdx.Comp σ),
      LazIdx.toM τ (LazIdx.transition h x) = LazIdx.toM σ x := by
    intro σ τ h x
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
    rfl
  refine ⟨LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (Module.DirectLimit.lift R (LazIdx R M) LazIdx.Comp (fun σ τ h => LazIdx.transition h)
      LazIdx.toM Hcompat) ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · -- injective
    rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨σ, x, rfl⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.exists_of z
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
    rw [Module.DirectLimit.lift_of] at hz
    have hvker : (v : (M × ℕ) →₀ R) ∈
        LinearMap.ker (Finsupp.linearCombination R (Prod.fst : M × ℕ → M)) := hz
    set σ' : LazIdx R M :=
      ⟨σ.J, σ.N ⊔ Submodule.span R {(v : (M × ℕ) →₀ R)},
        σ.hNfg.sup (Submodule.fg_span_singleton _),
        sup_le σ.hNK ((Submodule.span_singleton_le_iff_mem _ _).mpr hvker),
        sup_le σ.hNJ ((Submodule.span_singleton_le_iff_mem _ _).mpr v.property)⟩
    have hσσ' : σ ≤ σ' := ⟨subset_refl _, le_sup_left⟩
    have htrans0 : LazIdx.transition hσσ' (Submodule.Quotient.mk v) = 0 := by
      rw [LazIdx.transition_mk, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, LazIdx.mem_sub]
      exact Submodule.mem_sup_right (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self _)
    rw [← Module.DirectLimit.of_f (hij := hσσ'), htrans0, map_zero]
  · -- surjective
    intro m
    set σ₀ : LazIdx R M :=
      ⟨{(m, 0)}, ⊥, Submodule.fg_bot, bot_le, bot_le⟩ with hσ₀
    set w : Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ₀.J : Set (M × ℕ)) :=
      ⟨Finsupp.single (m, 0) 1, Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 (by simp [hσ₀])⟩ with hw
    refine ⟨Module.DirectLimit.of R (LazIdx R M) LazIdx.Comp
      (fun σ τ h => LazIdx.transition h) σ₀ (Submodule.Quotient.mk w), ?_⟩
    rw [Module.DirectLimit.lift_of, LazIdx.toM_mk, hw, Finsupp.linearCombination_single,
      one_smul]

/-- Two linear maps out of `R^s` agreeing on all basis vectors `e_z` (`z ∈ s`) are equal. -/
theorem Finsupp.supported_linearMap_ext {α : Type*} (s : Set α) {P : Type*} [AddCommGroup P]
    [Module R P]
    (F G : (Finsupp.supported R R s) →ₗ[R] P)
    (h : ∀ (z : α) (hz : z ∈ s),
        F ⟨Finsupp.single z 1, Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 hz⟩
          = G ⟨Finsupp.single z 1, Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 hz⟩) :
    F = G := by
  set e := Finsupp.supportedEquivFinsupp (M := R) (R := R) s with he
  have key :
      F ∘ₗ (e.symm : (↥s →₀ R) →ₗ[R] _) = G ∘ₗ (e.symm : (↥s →₀ R) →ₗ[R] _) := by
    apply Finsupp.lhom_ext'
    intro z
    apply LinearMap.ext_ring
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Finsupp.lsingle_apply]
    have hz1 : (e.symm (Finsupp.single z (1:R)) : Finsupp.supported R R s)
        = ⟨Finsupp.single (z : α) 1, Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 z.property⟩ := by
      apply Subtype.ext
      rw [he, Finsupp.supportedEquivFinsupp_symm_single]
    show F (e.symm (Finsupp.single z 1)) = G (e.symm (Finsupp.single z 1))
    rw [hz1]; exact h (z : α) z.property
  apply LinearMap.ext
  intro v
  have : v = e.symm (e v) := (e.symm_apply_apply v).symm
  rw [this]
  exact LinearMap.congr_fun key (e v)

/-- Two linear maps out of a finsupp module agreeing on all `single a 1` are equal. -/
private theorem lhom_ext_single_one {α P : Type*} [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P]
    {F G : (α →₀ R) →ₗ[R] P} (h : ∀ a, F (Finsupp.single a 1) = G (Finsupp.single a 1)) :
    F = G :=
  Finsupp.basisSingleOne.ext h

/-- For flat `M`, every index of the `(J,N)` system lies below one whose component is free
and finite. -/
theorem LazIdx.exists_free_finite_le [Module.Flat R M] :
    ∀ σ : LazIdx R M, ∃ τ : LazIdx R M,
      (Module.Free R (LazIdx.Comp τ) ∧ Module.Finite R (LazIdx.Comp τ)) ∧ σ ≤ τ := by
  classical
  intro σ
  obtain ⟨k, a, y, hya⟩ :=
    Module.Flat.exists_factorization_of_finitePresentation (M := M) (LazIdx.toM σ)
  set q : (Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))) →ₗ[R] LazIdx.Comp σ :=
    (LazIdx.sub σ).mkQ with hq
  -- coefficient function: cls z = a (q e_z) for z ∈ σ.J, else 0
  set cls : (M × ℕ) → (Fin k →₀ R) :=
    fun z => if hz : z ∈ σ.J then a (q ⟨Finsupp.single z 1, Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 hz⟩)
      else 0 with hcls
  -- fresh coordinates
  set n0 := σ.J.sup (·.snd) with hn0
  set coord : Fin k → M × ℕ := fun t => (y (Finsupp.single t 1), n0 + 1 + t.val) with hcoord
  have hinj : Function.Injective coord := by
    intro s t hst
    have : n0 + 1 + s.val = n0 + 1 + t.val := congrArg Prod.snd hst
    exact Fin.ext (by omega)
  have hout : ∀ t, coord t ∉ σ.J := by
    intro t hmem
    have h2 : (coord t).snd ≤ σ.J.sup (·.snd) := Finset.le_sup (f := (·.snd)) hmem
    simp only [hcoord] at h2; omega
  -- forward coefficient w
  set w : (M × ℕ) → (Fin k →₀ R) :=
    fun z => if h : ∃ t, coord t = z then Finsupp.single h.choose 1 else cls z with hw
  have hwcoord : ∀ t, w (coord t) = Finsupp.single t 1 := by
    intro t
    have hex : ∃ s, coord s = coord t := ⟨t, rfl⟩
    rw [hw]; simp only [hex, dite_eq_left]
    congr 1; exact hinj hex.choose_spec
  have hwJ : ∀ z ∈ σ.J, w z = cls z := by
    intro z hz
    rw [hw]
    have hnex : ¬ ∃ t, coord t = z := by
      rintro ⟨t, rfl⟩; exact hout t hz
    simp only [hnex, dite_eq_right, not_false_iff]
  -- the maps A and Bmap
  set A : ((M × ℕ) →₀ R) →ₗ[R] (Fin k →₀ R) := Finsupp.linearCombination R w with hA
  set Bmap : (Fin k →₀ R) →ₗ[R] ((M × ℕ) →₀ R) := Finsupp.lmapDomain R R coord with hBmap
  have hAB : A.comp Bmap = LinearMap.id := by
    refine lhom_ext_single_one fun t => ?_
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.id_coe, id_eq]
    rw [hBmap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply, Finsupp.mapDomain_single, hA,
      Finsupp.linearCombination_single, hwcoord, one_smul]
  -- relation generators
  set r : (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ)) → ((M × ℕ) →₀ R) :=
    fun x => Finsupp.single (x : M × ℕ) 1 - Bmap (cls (x : M × ℕ)) with hr
  set Nrel : Submodule R ((M × ℕ) →₀ R) := Submodule.span R (Set.range r) with hNrel
  set J' : Finset (M × ℕ) := σ.J ∪ Finset.image coord Finset.univ with hJ'
  set N' : Submodule R ((M × ℕ) →₀ R) := σ.N ⊔ Nrel with hN'
  have hcls_e : ∀ z (hz : z ∈ σ.J),
      cls z = a (q ⟨Finsupp.single z 1, Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 hz⟩) :=
    fun z hz => by simp only [hcls, dite_eq_left hz]
  -- A on single z 1
  have hAsingle : ∀ z, A (Finsupp.single z 1) = w z := by
    intro z; rw [hA, Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul]
  -- A restricted to supported σ.J equals a ∘ q
  have hAsub : A.comp (Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ))).subtype = a.comp q := by
    apply Finsupp.supported_linearMap_ext
    intro z hz
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply]
    rw [hAsingle z, hwJ z (Finset.mem_coe.mp hz), hcls_e z (Finset.mem_coe.mp hz)]
  -- π ∘ Bmap = y
  set π : ((M × ℕ) →₀ R) →ₗ[R] M := Finsupp.linearCombination R (Prod.fst : M × ℕ → M) with hπ
  have hπB : π.comp Bmap = y := by
    refine lhom_ext_single_one fun t => ?_
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply]
    rw [hBmap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply, Finsupp.mapDomain_single, hπ,
      Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul, hcoord]
  -- σ.N ≤ ker A
  have hAN : σ.N ≤ LinearMap.ker A := by
    intro v hv
    have hvJ : v ∈ Finsupp.supported R R (↑σ.J : Set (M × ℕ)) := σ.hNJ hv
    have e1 : A v = a (q ⟨v, hvJ⟩) := LinearMap.congr_fun hAsub ⟨v, hvJ⟩
    have hq0 : q ⟨v, hvJ⟩ = 0 := by
      rw [hq, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, LazIdx.mem_sub]; exact hv
    rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, e1, hq0, map_zero]
  -- A (r x) = 0
  have hAr : ∀ x, A (r x) = 0 := by
    intro x
    rw [hr]
    simp only [map_sub, hAsingle]
    have hclsx : w (x : M × ℕ) = cls (x : M × ℕ) := hwJ (x : M × ℕ) x.property
    rw [hclsx]
    rw [show A (Bmap (cls (x : M × ℕ))) = cls (x : M × ℕ) from LinearMap.congr_fun hAB _, sub_self]
  -- σ.J ⊆ J'
  have hσJ' : σ.J ⊆ J' := by rw [hJ']; exact Finset.subset_union_left
  -- coord t ∈ J'
  have hcoordJ' : ∀ t, coord t ∈ J' := by
    intro t; rw [hJ']
    exact Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨t, Finset.mem_univ t, rfl⟩)
  -- Bmap lands in supported (range coord)
  have hBsupp : ∀ v, Bmap v ∈ Finsupp.supported R R (Set.range coord) := by
    intro v
    rw [hBmap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply, Finsupp.mem_supported]
    refine le_trans (Finsupp.mapDomain_support) ?_
    intro z hz
    simp only [Finset.coe_image, Set.mem_image] at hz
    obtain ⟨a', _, rfl⟩ := hz
    exact ⟨a', rfl⟩
  -- range coord ⊆ J'
  have hrangeJ' : (Set.range coord) ⊆ (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ)) := by
    rintro z ⟨t, rfl⟩; exact Finset.mem_coe.mpr (hcoordJ' t)
  -- r x ∈ supported J'
  have hrJ' : ∀ x, r x ∈ Finsupp.supported R R (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ)) := by
    intro x
    rw [hr]
    exact Submodule.sub_mem _
      (Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 (Finset.mem_coe.mpr (hσJ' x.property)))
      (Finsupp.supported_mono hrangeJ' (hBsupp (cls (x : M × ℕ))))
  have hNrel_le : ∀ {S : Submodule R ((M × ℕ) →₀ R)}, (∀ x, r x ∈ S) → Nrel ≤ S :=
    fun h => Submodule.span_le.2 (Set.range_subset_iff.2 h)
  -- Nrel ≤ supported J'
  have hNrelJ' : Nrel ≤ Finsupp.supported R R (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ)) := hNrel_le hrJ'
  -- π (r x) = 0
  have hπr : ∀ x, π (r x) = 0 := by
    intro x
    rw [hr, map_sub]
    have h1 : π (Finsupp.single (x : M × ℕ) 1) = (x : M × ℕ).fst := by
      rw [hπ, Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul]
    rw [h1, show π (Bmap (cls (x : M × ℕ))) = _ from LinearMap.congr_fun hπB _]
    -- y (cls x.1) = LazIdx.toM σ (q e_x) = x.1.1
    have hLaz : LazIdx.toM σ
        (q ⟨Finsupp.single (x : M × ℕ) 1, Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 x.property⟩) =
          (x : M × ℕ).fst := by
      rw [hq, Submodule.mkQ_apply, LazIdx.toM_mk, Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul]
    rw [hcls_e _ x.property, ← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← hya, hLaz, sub_self]
  -- Nrel ≤ ker π
  have hNrelK : Nrel ≤ LinearMap.ker π := hNrel_le hπr
  -- Nrel FG
  have hNrelFG : Nrel.FG := by
    rw [hNrel]
    exact Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_range r)
  -- N' ≤ ker A
  have hAN' : N' ≤ LinearMap.ker A := sup_le hAN (hNrel_le hAr)
  -- σ.N ≤ supported J' (for τ.hNJ first component)
  have hσNJ' : σ.N ≤ Finsupp.supported R R (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ)) :=
    le_trans σ.hNJ (Finsupp.supported_mono (by exact_mod_cast hσJ'))
  -- build τ
  set τ : LazIdx R M :=
    ⟨J', N', σ.hNfg.sup hNrelFG, sup_le σ.hNK hNrelK, sup_le hσNJ' hNrelJ'⟩ with hτ
  refine ⟨τ, ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ⟨hσJ', le_sup_left⟩⟩
  · -- freeness
    -- class map for τ
    set q' : (Finsupp.supported R R (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ))) →ₗ[R] LazIdx.Comp τ :=
      (LazIdx.sub τ).mkQ with hq'
    -- forward map φ : LazIdx.Comp τ → Fin k →₀ R
    have hφker : LazIdx.sub τ ≤
        LinearMap.ker (A.comp (Finsupp.supported R R (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ))).subtype) := by
      intro v hv
      rw [LazIdx.mem_sub] at hv
      rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply]
      exact hAN' (show (v : (M × ℕ) →₀ R) ∈ N' from hv)
    set φ : LazIdx.Comp τ →ₗ[R] (Fin k →₀ R) :=
      (LazIdx.sub τ).liftQ (A.comp (Finsupp.supported R R (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ))).subtype) hφker
        with hφ
    -- backward map ψ : Fin k →₀ R → LazIdx.Comp τ
    set ψ : (Fin k →₀ R) →ₗ[R] LazIdx.Comp τ :=
      Finsupp.linearCombination R (fun t => q' ⟨Finsupp.single (coord t) 1,
        Finsupp.single_mem_supported R 1 (Finset.mem_coe.mpr (hcoordJ' t))⟩) with hψ
    have hφq : ∀ v, φ (q' v) = A v := fun v => rfl
    -- φ ∘ ψ = id
    have hφψ : φ.comp ψ = LinearMap.id := by
      refine lhom_ext_single_one fun t => ?_
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.id_coe, id_eq]
      rw [hψ, Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul, hφq, hAsingle, hwcoord]
    -- ψ = mkQ ∘ (Bmap corestricted to supported J')
    set Bmap'' : (Fin k →₀ R) →ₗ[R] (Finsupp.supported R R (↑J' : Set (M × ℕ))) :=
      LinearMap.codRestrict _ Bmap (fun v => Finsupp.supported_mono hrangeJ' (hBsupp
          v)) with hBmap''
    have hψB : ψ = (LazIdx.sub τ).mkQ.comp Bmap'' := by
      rw [hψ]
      refine lhom_ext_single_one fun t => ?_
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul]
      rw [hq']
      congr 1
      apply Subtype.ext
      rw [hBmap'', LinearMap.codRestrict_apply]
      show Finsupp.single (coord t) 1 = (Bmap (Finsupp.single t 1) : (M × ℕ) →₀ R)
      rw [hBmap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply, Finsupp.mapDomain_single]
    -- ψ ∘ φ = id  (hence ψ surjective)
    have hψφ : ψ.comp φ = LinearMap.id := by
      have key : (ψ.comp φ).comp (LazIdx.sub τ).mkQ = (LazIdx.sub τ).mkQ := by
        apply Finsupp.supported_linearMap_ext
        intro z hz
        rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply]
        -- φ (mkQ e_z) = A e_z = w z
        rw [show (LazIdx.sub τ).mkQ _ = q' _ from rfl, hφq, hAsingle]
        -- ψ (w z) = mkQ e_z
        rw [hψB, LinearMap.comp_apply]
        -- mkQ (Bmap'' (w z)) = mkQ e_z, i.e. e_z - Bmap (w z) ∈ LazIdx.sub τ
        rw [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.eq]
        rw [LazIdx.sub, Submodule.mem_comap, map_sub, Submodule.subtype_apply,
          Submodule.subtype_apply, hBmap'', LinearMap.codRestrict_apply]
        show (Bmap (w z) - Finsupp.single z 1 : (M × ℕ) →₀ R) ∈ N'
        -- goal: Bmap (w z) - single z 1 ∈ N'.  Suffices: single z 1 - Bmap (w z) ∈ N'.
        rw [← neg_sub, Submodule.neg_mem_iff]
        by_cases hzc : ∃ t, coord t = z
        · -- z is a coord: single z 1 - Bmap (w z) = single z 1 - single z 1 = 0
          obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hzc
          rw [hwcoord, hBmap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply, Finsupp.mapDomain_single, sub_self]
          exact Submodule.zero_mem _
        · -- z ∈ σ.J: relation r ⟨z⟩ ∈ Nrel ⊆ N'
          have hzJ : z ∈ σ.J := by
            have hzJ' : z ∈ J' := Finset.mem_coe.mp hz
            rcases Finset.mem_union.mp (hJ' ▸ hzJ') with h | h
            · exact h
            · exact absurd (Finset.mem_image.mp h) (by rintro ⟨t, _, ht⟩; exact hzc ⟨t, ht⟩)
          have : Finsupp.single z 1 - Bmap (w z) = r ⟨z, Finset.mem_coe.mpr hzJ⟩ := by
            rw [hr]; congr 1; rw [hwJ z hzJ]
          rw [this, hN', hNrel]
          exact Submodule.mem_sup_right (Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, rfl⟩)
      exact Submodule.linearMap_qext _ key
    exact Module.Free.of_equiv (LinearEquiv.ofLinearMap ψ φ hψφ hφψ)
  · -- finite
    have := LazIdx.finitePresentation_comp τ
    infer_instance

end LazardSystem

open Module in
/-- If `M` is flat, it is the colimit of a directed system of finitely presented modules in
which the free finite components are cofinal.

The two properties must come from the same system: free-finite cofinality fails for an
arbitrary finitely presented system with colimit `M`, e.g. the constant system for the flat,
non-free module `M = R·(1,0)` over `R = ℤ × ℤ`. -/
theorem flat_exists_finitePresentation_system_free_cofinal {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (M : Type u)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Flat R M] :
    ∃ (ι : Type u) (_ : Preorder ι) (_ : IsDirected ι (· ≤ ·)) (_ : Nonempty ι)
      (_ : DecidableEq ι) (G : ι → Type u) (_ : (i : ι) → AddCommGroup (G i))
      (_ : (i : ι) → Module R (G i)) (f : (i j : ι) → i ≤ j → G i →ₗ[R] G j)
      (_ : DirectedSystem G fun i j h => f i j h),
      (∀ i, Module.FinitePresentation R (G i)) ∧
      (∀ i : ι, ∃ j : ι, (Module.Free R (G j) ∧ Module.Finite R (G j)) ∧ i ≤ j) ∧
        Nonempty (Module.DirectLimit G f ≃ₗ[R] M) :=
  ⟨LazIdx R M, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, lazDecEq, LazIdx.Comp,
    inferInstance, inferInstance, fun _ _ h => LazIdx.transition h, lazDirectedSystem,
    inferInstance, LazIdx.exists_free_finite_le, LazIdx.nonempty_directLimit_linearEquiv⟩

open Module in
/-- **Forward direction of Lazard's theorem.** If `M` is flat, then `M` is the colimit of a
directed system of free finite `R`-modules. -/
@[sga "3 VIIA 4.2.1" "more general",
  sga "4 V 8.2.12" "special case",
  sga "4 XVII 5.5.1.1" "commutative rings",
  sga "4 XVII 5.5.1.2" "partial",
  sga "4 XVII 5.5.6.3" "partial"]
theorem flat_exists_directLimit_free_finite {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (M : Type u)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Flat R M] :
    ∃ (ι' : Type u) (_ : Preorder ι') (_ : IsDirected ι' (· ≤ ·)) (_ : Nonempty ι')
      (_ : DecidableEq ι') (G' : ι' → Type u) (_ : (i : ι') → AddCommGroup (G' i))
      (_ : (i : ι') → Module R (G' i)) (f' : (i j : ι') → i ≤ j → G' i →ₗ[R] G' j)
      (_ : DirectedSystem G' fun i j h => f' i j h),
      (∀ i, Module.Free R (G' i)) ∧ (∀ i, Module.Finite R (G' i)) ∧
        Nonempty (Module.DirectLimit G' f' ≃ₗ[R] M) := by
  obtain ⟨ι, hpre, hdir, hne, hdec, G, hag, hmod, f, hds, -, hcof, ⟨e⟩⟩ :=
    flat_exists_finitePresentation_system_free_cofinal (R := R) M
  set P : ι → Prop := fun i => Module.Free R (G i) ∧ Module.Finite R (G i)
  have : DecidableEq {i : ι // P i} := Classical.decEq _
  have : Nonempty {i : ι // P i} := by
    obtain ⟨j, hj, _⟩ := hcof (Classical.arbitrary ι)
    exact ⟨⟨j, hj⟩⟩
  have hdir2 : IsDirected {i : ι // P i} (· ≤ ·) := by
    refine ⟨fun a b => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨c, hac, hbc⟩ := directed_of (· ≤ ·) a.val b.val
    obtain ⟨d, hd, hcd⟩ := hcof c
    exact ⟨⟨d, hd⟩, Subtype.coe_le_coe.mp (le_trans hac hcd),
      Subtype.coe_le_coe.mp (le_trans hbc hcd)⟩
  have hdssub : DirectedSystem (fun i : {i : ι // P i} => G i.val)
      (fun i j h => f i.val j.val h) :=
    { map_self := fun {i} x => DirectedSystem.map_self
        (f := fun i j h => (f i j h : G i → G j)) (i := i.val) x
      map_map := fun {i j k} hij hjk x => DirectedSystem.map_map
        (f := fun i j h => (f i j h : G i → G j)) hij hjk x }
  obtain ⟨ecof⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.nonempty_linearEquiv_of_cofinal (G := G) (f := f) P hcof
  exact ⟨{i : ι // P i}, inferInstance, hdir2, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    fun i => G i.val, fun i => hag i.val, fun i => hmod i.val, fun i j h => f i.val j.val h,
    hdssub, fun i => i.2.1, fun i => i.2.2, ⟨ecof.trans e⟩⟩

/-- **Lazard's theorem.**
An `R`-module `M` over a commutative ring `R` is flat if and only if `M` is the
colimit of a directed system of free finite `R`-modules: there exists a directed
(nonempty, filtered) preorder `ι`, a family of `R`-modules `G : ι → Type` with
`R`-linear transition maps `f` forming a `DirectedSystem`, such that every `G i`
is free and finite, together with an `R`-linear isomorphism between the direct
limit `Module.DirectLimit G f` and `M`. -/
@[stacks 058G,
  ega "0 6.1.2" "special case",
  ega "0 6.2.3" "special case",
  ega "0 6.3.4" "partial",
  sga "3 VIIA 4.2.1" "more general",
  sga "4 V 1.2" "Reverse implication only",
  sga "4 V 8.2.12" "special case",
  sga "4 VI 8.6.4" "special case",
  sga "4 XVII 5.5.1.1" "special case",
  sga "4 XVII 5.5.1.2" "partial",
  sga "4 XVII 5.5.6.3" "partial"]
theorem flat_iff_directLimit_free_finite {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (M : Type u)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] :
    Module.Flat R M ↔
      ∃ (ι : Type u) (_ : Preorder ι) (_ : IsDirected ι (· ≤ ·)) (_ : Nonempty ι)
        (_ : DecidableEq ι) (G : ι → Type u) (_ : (i : ι) → AddCommGroup (G i))
        (_ : (i : ι) → Module R (G i)) (f : (i j : ι) → i ≤ j → G i →ₗ[R] G j)
        (_ : DirectedSystem G fun i j h => f i j h),
        (∀ i, Module.Free R (G i)) ∧ (∀ i, Module.Finite R (G i)) ∧
          Nonempty (Module.DirectLimit G f ≃ₗ[R] M) := by
  refine ⟨fun _ => flat_exists_directLimit_free_finite M, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨ι, _, _, _, _, G, _, _, f, _, hfree, _, ⟨e⟩⟩
  have : Module.Flat R (Module.DirectLimit G f) := Module.Flat.directLimit
  exact Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv e.symm

end
